                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Such a painful experience. There's 3 ways to engage in combat: Melee, Range, and Magic. I went through the game using a sword which felt horrible. The damage felt good but you some enemies just ruined you because of how close you have to get and no ability to block appropriately (There's a shield but the amount of time to raise it inbetween swings makes it impossible to use effectively). The game had potential to be an OK action rpg but the combat was too troublesome to overlook. That alongside the flawed \"improvement\" system (You can upgrade your weapons/armor like in Maplestory 2 but if you fail once the entire goddamn thing is destroyed). Ontop of that there is NO story whatsoever, the main quests are about a sentence long and repeat every single time. Overall I wouldn't recommend this even as a free product.",
